1
00:00:00,191 --> 00:00:04,651
On Diwali night, when lakhs
of diyas light up together,

2
00:00:04,671 --> 00:00:07,278
which city shines the brightest?

3
00:00:08,656 --> 00:00:11,404
That city is Ayodhya, a name that means,

4
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:13,501
the one that no one can fight.

5
00:00:15,639 --> 00:00:19,558
Right on the banks of the Saryu,
this is the birthplace of Lord Ram.

6
00:00:20,362 --> 00:00:23,009
This is Ayodhya, Uttar Pradesh.

7
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:28,767
Here lives a story thousands of years
old, and a brand new temple too.

8
00:00:29,099 --> 00:00:31,087
Every lane here holds a story.

9
00:00:32,685 --> 00:00:37,716
So today, we will tell you
everything, from history to planning.

10
00:00:38,259 --> 00:00:41,724
Ayodhya was once the capital
of the Koshal kingdom.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,587
Raja Dasharath of the
Suryavansh ruled here.

12
00:00:45,861 --> 00:00:49,907
And right here, in his
home, Shri Ram was born.

13
00:00:50,282 --> 00:00:54,136
For centuries, this place has
been the heart of people's faith.

14
00:00:54,323 --> 00:00:58,136
Ayodhya is one of the seven
holy cities that grant moksha.

15
00:00:58,945 --> 00:01:03,318
Then, in August twenty twenty,
the bhoomi pujan took place.

16
00:01:03,566 --> 00:01:06,407
And within a few years,
the temple stood complete.

17
00:01:07,447 --> 00:01:10,383
On the twenty second of
January, twenty twenty four,

18
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:13,074
the Pran Pratishtha
happened at the Ram Mandir.

19
00:01:13,368 --> 00:01:17,359
The temple is built in the Nagara
style, with pink sandstone.

20
00:01:18,730 --> 00:01:21,914
It has three floors,
hundreds of pillars,

21
00:01:21,934 --> 00:01:24,279
and fine carving on every one.

22
00:01:24,751 --> 00:01:28,227
Inside, Ram Lalla sits
in his child form.

23
00:01:28,692 --> 00:01:31,887
The complex also has small
shrines of Surya, Ganesh,

24
00:01:31,907 --> 00:01:33,143
Shiv and Hanuman ji.

25
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:38,430
So, what can you see in a
single day? Believe me, a lot.

26
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:41,502
And I will tell you the cost at the end.

27
00:01:41,882 --> 00:01:45,802
First, visit the Ram Janmabhoomi
Mandir. Reach early in the morning,

28
00:01:45,822 --> 00:01:47,271
and the crowd is thinner.

29
00:01:49,367 --> 00:01:51,373
Then climb Hanuman Garhi.

30
00:01:51,393 --> 00:01:55,120
This hill temple sits
above seventy six steps.

31
00:01:55,911 --> 00:01:59,514
And from the top, the
whole city lies before you.

32
00:01:59,773 --> 00:02:04,042
The tradition here is simple.
First Hanuman ji's darshan,

33
00:02:04,062 --> 00:02:05,341
then Ram Lalla's.

34
00:02:07,139 --> 00:02:08,790
Next, Kanak Bhawan.

35
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:13,384
Queen Kaikeyi gave this
palace to Sita ji as a gift.

36
00:02:13,824 --> 00:02:17,230
In the golden sanctum,
stand Ram and Sita.

37
00:02:19,012 --> 00:02:23,868
Then Ram ki Paidi, where the evening
aarti happens on the Saryu ghats.

38
00:02:24,958 --> 00:02:29,045
Then Guptar Ghat. Right here,
Ram took his jal samadhi.

39
00:02:30,623 --> 00:02:34,814
During Deepotsav, these same
ghats glow with lakhs of diyas.

40
00:02:35,628 --> 00:02:38,725
And people come from far away
to watch the Saryu aarti.

41
00:02:40,245 --> 00:02:42,213
So remember these five places,

42
00:02:42,709 --> 00:02:44,156
Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir,

43
00:02:44,613 --> 00:02:45,597
Hanuman Garhi,

44
00:02:45,775 --> 00:02:46,679
Kanak Bhawan,

45
00:02:46,756 --> 00:02:47,963
Ram ki Paidi,

46
00:02:48,239 --> 00:02:49,461
and Guptar Ghat.

47
00:02:50,243 --> 00:02:53,355
Now the question is,
how do you get there?

48
00:02:53,903 --> 00:02:57,038
Ayodhya Dham Junction is just
two kilometres from the temple.

49
00:02:58,905 --> 00:03:03,598
There is also Ayodhya Cantt station,
about eleven kilometres away.

50
00:03:04,387 --> 00:03:09,207
From Lucknow, it is about one hundred
thirty five kilometres by road,

51
00:03:09,227 --> 00:03:10,560
around three hours.

52
00:03:12,031 --> 00:03:14,401
From cities like Lucknow and Varanasi,

53
00:03:14,421 --> 00:03:16,559
trains and buses are easy to find.

54
00:03:18,033 --> 00:03:19,061
And if you fly,

55
00:03:19,081 --> 00:03:24,813
the Maharishi Valmiki International Airport
is about ten kilometres from the city.

56
00:03:26,559 --> 00:03:29,844
From the station to the temple,
e-rickshaws are easy to find.

57
00:03:31,402 --> 00:03:34,582
There is no charge for
darshan at the Ram Mandir.

58
00:03:35,205 --> 00:03:38,804
Darshan timings are seven to
eleven thirty in the morning,

59
00:03:38,824 --> 00:03:40,821
and two to seven in the evening.

60
00:03:42,590 --> 00:03:46,000
On festivals and crowded days,
book your stay in advance.

61
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:52,269
And before you go, check the timings
once on the official website.

62
00:03:54,538 --> 00:03:57,457
The best season to visit
is October to March.

63
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:00,693
Now, let us plan one day.

64
00:04:01,322 --> 00:04:03,972
At six in the morning,
start by the Saryu.

65
00:04:05,805 --> 00:04:08,929
At seven, have darshan at
the Ram Janmabhoomi Mandir.

66
00:04:10,111 --> 00:04:11,950
At eleven, go to Kanak Bhawan.

67
00:04:13,252 --> 00:04:15,227
In the afternoon, climb Hanuman Garhi.

68
00:04:16,393 --> 00:04:19,439
And in the evening, watch
the aarti at Ram ki Paidi.

69
00:04:20,534 --> 00:04:22,803
Reach half an hour early for the aarti.

70
00:04:24,215 --> 00:04:28,548
And remember, you cannot carry
phones or bags inside the temple.

71
00:04:28,568 --> 00:04:30,677
You must keep them in a locker.

72
00:04:31,619 --> 00:04:33,934
Keep your clothes simple and modest.

73
00:04:34,181 --> 00:04:38,190
There are many steps, so
with elders, walk slowly.

74
00:04:39,145 --> 00:04:42,248
Carry a water bottle,
wear comfortable shoes,

75
00:04:42,268 --> 00:04:44,141
and keep a little patience.

76
00:04:45,931 --> 00:04:51,151
The truth is, Ayodhya is not
just a city. It is a feeling.

77
00:04:51,656 --> 00:04:54,566
The darshan line is long, but
our channel's line is short.

78
00:04:57,543 --> 00:05:00,840
So subscribe, and make
it a little longer.
